{"status":"ready","content":"Let's solve this step by step:\r\n\r\n1) First, calculate the mean (average) of the data set\r\n   • $\\bar{x} = \\frac{25 + 10 + 0 + 9 + (-1) + (-14) + (-21)}{7}$\r\n   • $\\bar{x} = \\frac{-2}{7}$\r\n   • $\\bar{x} = -\\frac{2}{7}$\r\n\r\n2) Calculate the squared differences from the mean\r\n   • $(25 - (-\\frac{2}{7}))^2 = (25 + \\frac{2}{7})^2 = (\\frac{177}{7})^2 = 31,329/49$\r\n   • $(10 - (-\\frac{2}{7}))^2 = (10 + \\frac{2}{7})^2 = (\\frac{72}{7})^2 = 5,184/49$\r\n   • $(0 - (-\\frac{2}{7}))^2 = (0 + \\frac{2}{7})^2 = (\\frac{2}{7})^2 = 4/49$\r\n   • $(9 - (-\\frac{2}{7}))^2 = (9 + \\frac{2}{7})^2 = (\\frac{65}{7})^2 = 4,225/49$\r\n   • $(-1 - (-\\frac{2}{7}))^2 = (-1 + \\frac{2}{7})^2 = (-\\frac{5}{7})^2 = 25/49$\r\n   • $(-14 - (-\\frac{2}{7}))^2 = (-14 + \\frac{2}{7})^2 = (-\\frac{100}{7})^2 = 10,000/49$\r\n   • $(-21 - (-\\frac{2}{7}))^2 = (-21 + \\frac{2}{7})^2 = (-\\frac{149}{7})^2 = 22,201/49$\r\n\r\n3) Sum the squared differences\r\n   • $\\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})^2 = 31,329/49 + 5,184/49 + 4/49 + 4,225/49 + 25/49 + 10,000/49 + 22,201/49$\r\n   • $= 72,968/49$\r\n\r\n4) Divide by $(n-1) = 6$\r\n   • $\\frac{72,968/49}{6} = 2,041/49$\r\n\r\n5) Take the square root\r\n   • $\\sqrt{2,041/49} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2,041}}{7}$\r\n\r\n6) Therefore, $\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{2,041}}{7}}$\r\n\r\nThe answer is $\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{2,041}}{7}}$.\r\n","path":"responses/claude-3-5-haiku/livebench-065-math.txt","size":1298,"mtime":1779363928}